  "analytic": [
    "Signed complementary indices give remaining E weight1 for Q or2 for B when T=2. Actual final packet is V/U for Q, U for B; nonnegative weights then force exactly D^n,V,Q or D^n,U,B, with no later D. No C can remain in this E-clock3 stage. All earlier N/W/S stages are arbitrary.",
    "At source T2, V has A=B+2 and U has A=B. The exact affine endpoint equations force n=B+4 or B+3. First earlier W D gives B>=1. Therefore every proposed pop contains the last D,V,Q or D,U,B, regardless the unrestricted preceding history.",
    "Those suffixes delete a cell by D tick1 L and next require it at actual returned C tick1 L without any intervening read. This is a returned-C/complete-context contradiction, not a foreign-RAW grammar ban. Together with prior F T>=3, every spent portal has T>=3, so the earliest possible portal stays its original lifetime through this first return.",
    "For old source C2(VCC/UCC), the first W BASE is D-family, not necessarily a plain full D. Both D and DC have the necessary D+actual M11 prefix and both fail the same immutable read; for DC the conflicting read is owned C-tail tick1/read2, for D it is the next actual word tick1/read2. Thus the role exclusion is sound with this explicit qualification.",
    "The25 prescribed complete histories fail at their actual intended endpoint configurations, but they do not exhaust arbitrary W words or all T3 histories. Both genuine plain-source U-entry regression controls remain positive. No removed S run or withdrawn seal premise is used."
  ],
  "scope": "Three exact first returned raw-C residues only. Remaining old C roles C1 of DC/VC/UC after the separately signed C1-double-tail closure. No generic return closure, at-most-one spending, whole-ledger contraction or capture.",
